{
  "_comment": [
    "Viam 103 bimanual QC cell. Two ur5e arms inspect a stamped mailbox: arm-a picks it",
    "off the infeed belt by a flat side, presents the five faces its cup is not covering",
    "to inspect-cam, and sets it down on the handoff stand YAWED HALF A TURN; arm-b takes",
    "it from there, presents the remaining face, and places it in the good or bad tray",
    "according to the verdict the checks reach.",
    "",
    "The half turn is the whole design. The belt leaves only the +y approach at the pick,",
    "so arm-a's cup covers the part's +y face and the first check can never see it. Turned",
    "half a turn on the stand, that face swings round to arm-b's side: each arm works",
    "entirely on its own side of the cell, and arm-b ends up holding the opposite face of",
    "the part, which is what gives the second check something to do.",
    "",
    "Geometry started as the isaac-arcade layout scaled by 0.76 and is no longer only that:",
    "the trays and the camera have since been placed by hand against measured constraints,",
    "so rescaling would not move them correctly. What holds the layout together now is",
    "tests/test_cell_layout.py, which derives every station from THIS file and asserts the",
    "constraints - not the scale sweep.",
    "",
    "Those constraints, in the order they bit:",
    " - every station inside the arm's reach with ~10% margin, asserted at the flange and",
    "   at the APPROACH above it, which is higher and therefore further;",
    " - a reach bound of 1016.7 mm measured from the motion service, NOT the 850 mm on the",
    "   datasheet, which is to the wrist centre;",
    " - but a spherical bound is honest about position and silent about ORIENTATION: a tray",
    "   at 837 mm produced zero IK solutions because the tool could not point back along -y",
    "   from that far past the base. The trays therefore sit side by side in x at one y, so",
    "   both places use a configuration the cell has demonstrated;",
    " - arm-a cannot reach either tray holding the +y side, which is what makes the handoff",
    "   mandatory. Holding the other side it COULD reach the good tray - so it is the belt,",
    "   not the reach, that forces the handoff;",
    " - placing in one tray must not put arm-b's wrist inside the other. They used to sit",
    "   23 mm apart and it did.",
    "",
    "inspect-cam's fov_deg is NOT decoration - it defaults to 70 deg, and this cell sets",
    "50. Both arms present 1020 mm from the lens, where 50 deg horizontal frames 951 mm:",
    "1.35 px/mm at 1280 wide, which puts the narrowest defect mark - the 12 mm drip - at",
    "16 px across and 62 long. At the 70 deg default the same frame is 1428 mm wide, 0.90",
    "px/mm, and the 8 mm scratch is 7 px. Both arms are at 1020 mm because the camera aims",
    "at the MIDPOINT of the two presentation points rather than at the centreline, so the",
    "two checks frame the part alike and one threshold serves both.",
    "",
    "clipping_range_m is also not decoration, and its absence cost a day: usd's default",
    "near plane is 1.0 world unit - a metre - and the part is presented 780 mm away, so",
    "every frame rendered the part and the nearby arm links as pure black silhouettes while",
    "the wall behind came out fine. It reads as a lighting fault and is not one.",
    "",
    "The part carries its defects as children named defect_*, switched by visibility at",
    "runtime so a round is repeatable with no respawn. They spawn with collision: false,",
    "because usd visibility is a render attribute and physx keeps the collider either way -",
    "an invisible decal with a collider would sit in the other arm's approach and the",
    "suction raycast would hit it. Structural children DO collide. At least one defect must",
    "stay on the +y panel or the second check can never change a verdict.",
    "",
    "drive_damping_ratio on the arms is load-bearing. The ur5e asset's authored gains are",
    "stiffness ~5e5 against damping [21.7, 23.6, 234.5, 90.4, 3.5, 0.2] - about four orders",
    "short of critical, and 0.2 on the wrist roll. Those drives ring rather than settle, and",
    "a joint still ringing when a tolerance is checked is indistinguishable from one held by",
    "a collision. Every 'the wrist stalls short' in this project's notes was that.",
    "",
    "Each arm's isaac 'position' and its viam 'frame.translation' describe the same point",
    "in two units (m and mm), and the test keeps them consistent so the file reads",
    "honestly. Note they cannot actually disagree at runtime: apply_frame_to_attrs()",
    "overwrites 'position' from the frame, so the frame wins and 'position' is inert",
    "whenever a frame is present. The placement risk that IS real is rotational - whether",
    "the SVA's base frame and the Isaac USD's root share a yaw - and no config test can",
    "see it. Phase 1 settles it by commanding all-zero joints and comparing Isaac's",
    "end-effector world pose against motion.GetPose.",
    "",
    "end_effector_prim is what GetEndPosition reports; without it the call raises. The",
    "flange prim is also the one the yaw check compares against motion.GetPose.",
    "",
    "The 180 deg base yaw on each arm is load-bearing. A ur5e's zero configuration",
    "points its flange at about -164 deg in its own base frame, and every station in this",
    "cell is at +x, so unrotated the stations all need a pan within ~30 deg of the +-180",
    "wrap point. RDK seeds IK from the current configuration and scores by joint-space",
    "distance, so a workspace straddling the wrap ratchets: each move takes the nearest",
    "representative and the choice sticks. Facing the arms at the cell puts the stations",
    "near pan 0 and the discontinuity behind the arm, where nothing works.",
    "",
    "joint_limit_deg is load-bearing, not tuning. The ur5e SVA allows every revolute",
    "joint +-360 deg and the planner picks any solution in that range, so the cell winds",
    "itself up: measured over one pass of the stations a joint went from -26 to 206 deg,",
    "and after two passes an arm sat at 270. Near 360 it jams. 180 covers every",
    "orientation, and the solutions these stations need peak at 174 deg.",
    "",
    "shoulder_lift gets an explicit range because a symmetric limit puts the wrap point",
    "on every joint in the same place, and this joint's working range - about [-174, 4]",
    "- straddles 180. Bounded symmetrically it simply ratcheted there instead, sitting",
    "pinned at 180 over a long run. [-270, 90] still spans one turn, so there is exactly",
    "one solution per pose, but both ends are somewhere the arm never goes.",
    "",
    "The belt is derived from CONVEYOR_CENTER/CONVEYOR_SIZE, not eyeballed: it runs along",
    "y (0.258 x 0.836), which an earlier draft had transposed to run along x and centred",
    "on the pick slot instead of the belt. The trays are placed against the constraints above and tested; moving one needs test_cell_layout to stay green.",
    "",
    "None of this scenery exists in the frame system - props are spawned in Isaac only, so",
    "the planner cannot see the belt or the trays. qc:cell has to pass them as world_state",
    "obstacles on every move, or the arms will plan straight through them."
  ],
